{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RtewYC/translated_rust/CONFIGS.md; printf '\\\\n--- symbols summary ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,220p' /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RtewYC/translated_rust/SYMBOLS.md\"","aggregated_output":"# CONFIGS.md — the CONFIGURATION-SURFACE TABLE (valid inputs)\n\nMechanically derived from the branches the C actually takes.  Two kinds of axes:\n\n## Build-time axes (from `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`, `app/CMakeLists.txt`, `lib/*/CMakeLists.txt`)\n\n| CMake cache var | values | cargo feature | what it switches in the C |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `HASH_BACKEND` | `haraka`, `sha2`, `shake`, `blake` | `haraka`/`sha2`/`shake`/`blake` | which `lib/<HB>` is compiled and linked ⇒ which `hash_*.c` + `thash_*.c` provide `SPX_{initialize_hash_function,prf_addr,gen_message_random,hash_message,thash}`; also which `<HB>_offsets.h` supplies `SPX_OFFSET_*` (**sha2 uses a compressed 22-byte address layout, the other three use the plain 32-byte one**) and which `spx_ctx` members exist (`state_seeded[40]`(+`state_seeded_512[72]`) for sha2, `tweaked512_rc64[10][8]`+`tweaked256_rc32[10][8]` for haraka, nothing extra for shake/blake) |\n| `THASH` | `robust`, `simple` | `robust`/`simple` | `thash_<HB>_robust.c` (extra MGF1/`haraka_S` bitmask XORed into the input) vs `thash_<HB>_simple.c` |\n| `SECPAR` | `128s 128f 192s 192f 256s 256f` | `\"128s\"` … `\"256f\"` | `SPX_N` ∈ {16,24,32}, `SPX_FULL_HEIGHT`, `SPX_D`, `SPX_FORS_HEIGHT`, `SPX_FORS_TREES` ⇒ `SPX_TREE_HEIGHT`, `SPX_WOTS_LEN`, `SPX_FORS_*`, `SPX_BYTES`, and the derived `SPX_SHA512`/`SPX_BLAKE512` flag (`SPX_N >= 24`) which selects the 512-bit hash inside `thash` for `inblocks > 1` and inside `hash_*.c` |\n\n⇒ **4 × 2 × 6 = 48** build configurations.  Every row below is executed for\n**all 48**; `scripts/sweep_test.sh` drives that.\n\nPer-configuration constants (computed independently in\n`tests/common/mod.rs::cfg` from the cargo features and cross-checked against\nthe `.so`'s `crypto_sign_{bytes,publickeybytes,secretkeybytes,seedbytes}`):\n\n| secpar | N | FULL_H | D | TREE_H | FORS_H | FORS_T | WOTS_LEN | FORS_MSG_B | FORS_B | SPX_BYTES | 512-hash? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 128s | 16 | 63 | 7  | 9 | 12 | 14 | 35 | 21  | 2912  | 7856  | no  |\n| 128f | 16 | 66 | 22 | 3 | 6  | 33 | 35 | 25  | 3696  | 17088 | no  |\n| 192s | 24 | 63 | 7  | 9 | 14 | 17 | 51 | 30  | 6120  | 16224 | yes |\n| 192f | 24 | 66 | 22 | 3 | 8  | 33 | 51 | 33  | 7128  | 35664 | yes |\n| 256s | 32 | 64 | 8  | 8 | 14 | 22 | 67 | 39  | 10560 | 29792 | yes |\n| 256f | 32 | 68 | 17 | 4 | 9  | 35 | 67 | 40  | 11200 | 49856 | yes |\n\n## Runtime axes the C branches on\n\n| axis | where the C branches | distinct values that matter |\n|---|---|---|\n| `inblocks` | `thash_blake_*.c:23`, `thash_sha2_*.c:23` (`inblocks > 1` ⇒ 512-variant, only when `SPX_{BLAKE,SHA}512`); `thash_haraka_*.c:21/23` (`inblocks == 1` ⇒ `haraka512`/F-function, else `haraka_S`); shake: no branch | `0, 1, 2, 3, SPX_WOTS_LEN, SPX_FORS_TREES` |\n| `mlen` | `hash_sha2.c:94` (`SPX_N + mlen < SPX_SHAX_BLOCK_BYTES`), `hash_sha2.c:156` (`SPX_N+SPX_PK_BYTES+mlen < SPX_INBLOCKS*BLOCK`); `blake{256,512}_update`'s `left && ((datalen>>3)&0x3F) >= fill` and `blake*_final`'s `buflen == 440/888`, `< 440/888`, `> 440/888`; `keccak_inc_absorb`/`haraka_S_inc_absorb` rate boundaries (136 / 32) | `0,1,2,15,16,17,31,32,33,47,48,49,54,55,56,63,64,65,71,72,73,95,96,97,103,104,105,111,112,119,120,127,128,129,135,136,137,167,168,169,255,256,257,272,273,1000,4096` |\n| `leaf_idx` parity / value | `compute_root`'s `leaf_idx & 1` at every level; `treehash`'s `(leaf_idx^1)==idx`; `wots/fors_treehashx1`'s `(internal_idx ^ internal_leaf)==1`, `(internal_idx&1)==0 && idx<max_idx` | every `0 .. 2^tree_height-1` for small heights; random for large; plus the `~0u` \"no auth path\" sentinel |\n| `idx_offset` | `compute_root` (`idx_offset >>= 1`), `treehash` (`idx_offset >> (h+1)`), `*_treehashx1` (`internal_idx_offset >>= 1`) | `0`, `i*2^FORS_HEIGHT` for `i = 0..FORS_TREES-1`, random `u32` |\n| `tree_height` | loop bound of `compute_root` / `treehash` / `*_treehashx1` | `1, 2, 3, SPX_FORS_HEIGHT, SPX_TREE_HEIGHT` |\n| `info->wots_sign_leaf` | `wotsx1.c:28` (`leaf_idx == wots_sign_leaf` ⇒ emit signature, else `wots_k_mask=~0`) | equal to `leaf_idx` (signing) / different (pk-only) / `~0u` |\n| `info->wots_steps[i]` | `wotsx1.c:41,57` (`k == wots_k`) | every value `0 .. SPX_WOTS_W-1` (from `chain_lengths`), plus `>= SPX_WOTS_W` (never matches ⇒ no sig byte) |\n| `msg` for `chain_lengths` | `base_w` digit extraction + `wots_checksum` | random `SPX_N`-byte messages, all-`0x00`, all-`0xFF` (min/max checksum) |\n| `addr[8]` contents | `thash`/`prf_addr` hash the raw 32 (or 22) address bytes | random `u32[8]`, all-zero, all-`0xFFFFFFFF` |\n| `set_*` argument ranges | `address.c` truncation to `u8` vs full `u32`/`u64` | see `ERRORS.md` E21–E27 |\n| `outlen`/`inlen` of the MGF1s | `mgf1_*` / `blake*_mgf1` loop `(i+1)*OUT <= outlen` | `0,1,31,32,33,63,64,65,127,128,129, SPX_DGST_BYTES, inblocks*SPX_N` |\n| `outlen` of the sponges | `shake256_inc_squeeze`, `haraka_S_inc_squeeze`, `shake256_squeezeblocks` | `0,1,31,32,33,135,136,137,271,272,273` |\n| `inlen` of `sha*_inc_finalize` | padding needs an extra block when `inlen % BLOCK >= BLOCK-8` | `0 … 200` exhaustively |\n| `inblocks` of `sha*_inc_blocks` | `0, 1, 2, 5` | |\n| `xlen` of `randombytes`/`seedexpander` | `xlen > 15` vs `<= 15`; `xlen <= 16-buffer_pos` | `0,1,15,16,17,31,32,33,48,49,64,100` |\n| `maxlen`/`length_remaining` of `seedexpander_init`/`seedexpander` | `maxlen >= 0x100000000`; `xlen >= length_remaining` | see E05–E11 |\n| `SPX_D == 1`? | `hash_*.c:113/186/88/86` (`if (SPX_D == 1) *tree = 0;`) | **no shipped parameter set has `SPX_D == 1`** (min is 7), so only the `else` branch is reachable; documented, and the Rust keeps the same `if` |\n\n## The rows\n\n`entry point(s)` names the exported symbol(s) driven directly through `dlsym`.\nEvery row uses **many randomized inputs** from a fixed-seed SplitMix64 PRNG\n(see `tests/common/mod.rs::Rng`), not one hand-picked value.  Rows are grouped\nbottom-up: pure helpers → hash primitives → `thash`/`prf` → tree builders →\nWOTS/FORS → hypertree → the `api.h` one-shot wrappers.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | test | ✔ |\n|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|------|---|\n| **B01** | `SPX_ull_to_bytes` | `outlen ∈ {0,1,2,…,16}` × `in ∈ {0, 1, 0xFF, 0x100, u32::MAX, u64::MAX, 512 random u64}`; output buffer pre-filled with `0xAA` so untouched bytes are visible | `b01_ull_to_bytes` | [x] |\n| **B02** | `SPX_u32_to_bytes` | `in ∈ {0, 1, 0xFF, 0x100, 0xFFFF, u32::MAX, 512 random}`; buffer pre-filled `0xAA` | `b02_u32_to_bytes` | [x] |\n| **B03** | `SPX_bytes_to_ull` | `inlen ∈ {0,…,12}` × 512 random 12-byte inputs + all-`0x00` + all-`0xFF` (covers the `shift ≥ 64` case) | `b03_bytes_to_ull` | [x] |\n| **B04** | all 10 `SPX_set_*` / `SPX_copy_*` address functions | plain **and** sha2 (compressed) offset layouts (chosen by the backend feature); each called on an address pre-filled with random bytes, so both the written field *and* the 31 untouched bytes are compared; arguments span the full type range | `b04_address_all` | [x] |\n| **B05** | `SPX_copy_subtree_addr`, `SPX_copy_keypair_addr` | random `in`, random pre-filled `out`; verifies exactly `SPX_OFFSET_TREE+8` bytes (+ 4 at `SPX_OFFSET_KP_ADDR`) move | `b05_address_copy` | [x] |\n| **B06** | `blake256`, `blake256_init/update/final`, `blake256_compress` (blake only) | one-shot over `inlen ∈ {0,…,200} ∪ {255,256,257,300,400,1000,1024}`; incremental: split the input at **every** offset and compare the full 128-byte `blakestate256` **after every `init`/`update`/`final` call**; `blake256_final` reached with `buflen` `< 440`, `== 440`, `> 440`; plus 256 raw `blake256_compress` calls with a randomized `t`/`s`/`nullt` so both `nullt` branches are hit. (No \"incremental == one-shot\" assertion: `blake*_update` is not a general streaming API — see `ERRORS.md` N2.) | `b06_blake256` | [x] |\n| **B07** | `blake512`, `blake512_init/update/final`, `blake512_compress`, `cst` (blake only) | as B06 but with the 888/1024-bit boundaries and the 248-byte `blakestate512`; also asserts the exported `cst[16]` data symbol is identical in both `.so`s | `b07_blake512` | [x] |\n| **B08** | `SPX_blake256_mgf1`, `SPX_blake512_mgf1` (blake only) | `inlen ∈ {0,1,16,32,48,64,100}` × `outlen ∈ {0,1,31,32,33,63,64,65,96,127,128,129,200}` | `b08_blake_mgf1` | [x] |\n| **B09** | `sha256`, `sha256_inc_init/blocks/finalize` (sha2 only) | `inlen 0..200` one-shot; `inc_blocks(inblocks ∈ {0,1,2,5})` then `inc_finalize(inlen 0..200)`; covers the `inlen%64 ∈ {55,56,57,63}` padding boundary | `b09_sha256` | [x] |\n| **B10** | `sha512`, `sha512_inc_init/blocks/finalize` (sha2 only) | as B09 with the 128-byte block / `inlen%128 ∈ {111,112,113,127}` boundary | `b10_sha512` | [x] |\n| **B11** | `SPX_mgf1_256`, `SPX_mgf1_512` (sha2 only) | `inlen ∈ {0,1,16,32,48,54,64,100}` × `outlen ∈ {0,1,31,32,33,63,64,65,96,127,128,129,200}` | `b11_sha2_mgf1` | [x] |\n| **B12** | `SPX_seed_state` (sha2 only) | 256 random `pub_seed`; compares the **whole** `spx_ctx` byte image afterwards (`state_seeded[40]` and, when `SPX_SHA512`, `state_seeded_512[72]`) | `b12_seed_state` | [x] |\n| **B13** | `shake256`, `shake256_absorb`, `shake256_squeezeblocks` (shake only) | `inlen ∈ 0..300` × `outlen ∈ {0,1,31,32,33,135,136,137,271,272,273,500}`; `squeezeblocks(nblocks ∈ {0,1,2,3})` | `b13_shake256` | [x] |\n| **B14** | `shake256_inc_init/absorb/finalize/squeeze` (shake only) | absorb the same message in every 1-, 2- and 3-way split (crossing the 136-byte rate), squeeze in every 1- and 2-way split; compare against the one-shot `shake256` | `b14_shake256_inc` | [x] |\n| **B15** | `SPX_tweak_constants`, and `SPX_haraka512_perm`, `SPX_haraka512`, `SPX_haraka256` (haraka only) | 256 random `pub_seed`/`sk_seed`; compares the whole 2·N+960-byte `spx_ctx` image, then 512 random 64/32-byte inputs through each permutation | `b15_haraka_core` | [x] |\n| **B16** | `SPX_haraka_S`, `SPX_haraka_S_inc_init/absorb/finalize/squeeze` (haraka only) | `inlen ∈ 0..200` × `outlen ∈ {0,1,31,32,33,63,64,65,100}`; incremental absorb/squeeze split at every offset (crossing the 32-byte rate) | `b16_haraka_sponge` | [x] |\n| **B17** | `SPX_initialize_hash_function` | 256 random `(pub_seed, sk_seed)`; the **entire** `spx_ctx` image is compared, so this covers `seed_state` (sha2), `tweak_constants` (haraka) and the no-ops (shake/blake) | `b17_initialize_hash_function` | [x] |\n| **B18** | `SPX_prf_addr` | 512 random `(pub_seed, sk_seed, addr[8])` after `initialize_hash_function`; plus all-zero and all-`0xFF` addresses | `b18_prf_addr` | [x] |\n| **B19** | `SPX_thash`, `inblocks = 1` | `robust` **and** `simple`; 512 random `(ctx, addr, in)`; this is the F-function path (haraka: `haraka512`; blake/sha2: 256-variant even when `SPX_N ≥ 24`) | `b19_thash_1` | [x] |\n| **B20** | `SPX_thash`, `inblocks = 2` | 512 random inputs — the tree-node path; **first `inblocks > 1`, so it selects `blake512`/`sha512` when `SPX_N ≥ 24`, and `haraka_S` for haraka** | `b20_thash_2` | [x] |\n| **B21** | `SPX_thash`, `inblocks = 3` | 512 random inputs — an `inblocks` the library itself never uses, exercising the same 512/`haraka_S` path with a different length | `b21_thash_3` | [x] |\n| **B22** | `SPX_thash`, `inblocks = SPX_WOTS_LEN` | 256 random inputs — the WOTS-pk compression path (35/51/67 blocks) | `b22_thash_wots_len` | [x] |\n| **B23** | `SPX_thash`, `inblocks = SPX_FORS_TREES` | 256 random inputs — the FORS-pk compression path (14/33/17/33/22/35 blocks) | `b23_thash_fors_trees` | [x] |\n| **B24** | `SPX_thash`, `inblocks = 0` | 256 random inputs — see `ERRORS.md` E33 | `b24_thash_0` | [x] |\n| **B24b** | `SPX_thash`, `inblocks ∈ {4,5,7,8,16,17,33,64}` | 32 random inputs each — lengths no shipped parameter set uses, to pin the length arithmetic and the `>1`/`==1` dispatch | `b24b_thash_misc_inblocks` | [x] |\n| **B25** | `SPX_gen_message_random` | 74 message lengths from `0` to `4096` spanning every rate/block boundary of all four backends × 8 random `(sk_prf, optrand)`; the sha2 backend takes a different code path below/above `SPX_SHAX_BLOCK_BYTES - SPX_N`. The output buffer is over-sized because the blake backend writes 32/64 bytes rather than `SPX_N` (`ERRORS.md` N3), and both sides must touch the same number of bytes | `b25_gen_message_random` | [x] |\n| **B26** | `SPX_hash_message` | same 74 message lengths × 8 random `(R, pk)`; compares `digest[SPX_FORS_MSG_BYTES]`, `*tree` **and** `*leaf_idx` (the two masked integer outputs) and asserts both stay inside their documented ranges | `b26_hash_message` | [x] |\n| **B27** | `SPX_chain_lengths` | 512 random `SPX_N`-byte messages + all-`0x00` + all-`0xFF`; compares all `SPX_WOTS_LEN` `unsigned int` outputs (base-w digits **and** the 2/3-digit checksum) | `b27_chain_lengths` | [x] |\n| **B28** | `SPX_wots_gen_leafx1`, signing leaf | `leaf_idx == info.wots_sign_leaf`; random `ctx`, `leaf_addr`, `pk_addr`, and `wots_steps` taken from `chain_lengths` of a random message; compares `dest[SPX_N]` **and** the `SPX_WOTS_BYTES` signature buffer | `b28_wots_gen_leafx1_sign` | [x] |\n| **B29** | `SPX_wots_gen_leafx1`, non-signing leaf | `leaf_idx != info.wots_sign_leaf`, `wots_sig = NULL` (see E18); also `wots_sign_leaf = ~0u` | `b29_wots_gen_leafx1_pk` | [x] |\n| **B30** | `SPX_wots_gen_leafx1`, `wots_steps` out of range | every `wots_steps[i] = SPX_WOTS_W` … `0xFFFFFFFF` (`k == wots_k` never fires) | `b30_wots_gen_leafx1_steps_oor` | [x] |\n| **B31** | `SPX_wots_pk_from_sig` | 256 random `(sig[SPX_WOTS_BYTES], msg[SPX_N], ctx, addr)`; also `msg` all-`0x00` (max chain work) and all-`0xFF` (min) | `b31_wots_pk_from_sig` | [x] |\n| **B32** | `SPX_compute_root` | `tree_height ∈ {1,2,3,SPX_FORS_HEIGHT,SPX_TREE_HEIGHT}` × **every** `leaf_idx ∈ 0..2^h` for `h ≤ 4` and 64 random for larger × `idx_offset ∈ {0, random}`; compares `root` **and** the mutated `addr[8]` | `b32_compute_root` | [x] |\n| **B33** | `SPX_treehash` (function-pointer form) | `gen_leaf = SPX_fors_gen_leafx1` from the *same* library; `tree_height ∈ {1,2,3,SPX_FORS_HEIGHT}` × `leaf_idx` all values (+`~0u`) × `idx_offset ∈ {0, i·2^h, random}`; compares `root`, the full `auth_path` and the mutated `tree_addr` | `b33_treehash` | [x] |\n| **B34** | `SPX_fors_gen_leafx1` | 512 random `(ctx, info.leaf_addrx, addr_idx)` incl. `addr_idx = 0` and `0xFFFFFFFF`; compares `leaf` **and** the mutated `info` | `b34_fors_gen_leafx1` | [x] |\n| **B35** | `SPX_fors_treehashx1` | `tree_height = SPX_FORS_HEIGHT`; `leaf_idx` = all values for `FORS_HEIGHT ≤ 4`, 64 random otherwise, plus `~0u`; `idx_offset = i·2^FORS_HEIGHT` for all `i < SPX_FORS_TREES` plus random; compares `root`, `auth_path`, `tree_addr`, `info` | `b35_fors_treehashx1` | [x] |\n| **B36** | `SPX_wots_treehashx1` | `tree_height = SPX_TREE_HEIGHT`; `leaf_idx` = all values when `2^h ≤ 16`, else 8 random, plus `~0u` (with `wots_sig = NULL`); compares `root`, `auth_path`, the `SPX_WOTS_BYTES` sig, `tree_addr` and `info` | `b36_wots_treehashx1` | [x] |\n| **B37** | `SPX_fors_sign` | 256 random `(ctx, mhash[SPX_FORS_MSG_BYTES], fors_addr[8])` + all-`0x00`/all-`0xFF` mhash (min/max FORS indices); compares `sig[SPX_FORS_BYTES]` **and** `pk[SPX_N]` | `b37_fors_sign` | [x] |\n| **B38** | `SPX_fors_pk_from_sig` | 256 random `(sig, mhash, ctx, fors_addr)`, **plus** the `sig` produced by `SPX_fors_sign` (round-trip: `pk` must equal `fors_sign`'s `pk`) | `b38_fors_pk_from_sig` | [x] |\n| **B39** | `SPX_merkle_sign` | 128 random `(ctx, wots_addr, tree_addr, root)` × `idx_leaf ∈ {0, 1, 2^TREE_H-1, random, ~0u}`; compares the `SPX_WOTS_BYTES + SPX_TREE_HEIGHT*SPX_N` signature, the new `root` and both mutated addresses | `b39_merkle_sign` | [x] |\n| **B40** | `SPX_merkle_gen_root` | 128 random `(pub_seed, sk_seed)` after `initialize_hash_function` | `b40_merkle_gen_root` | [x] |\n| **B41** | `crypto_sign_secretkeybytes`, `crypto_sign_publickeybytes`, `crypto_sign_bytes`, `crypto_sign_seedbytes` | no input; also cross-checked against the constants derived independently in the test from the cargo features | `b41_sizes` | [x] |\n| **B42** | `crypto_sign_seed_keypair` | 64 random `3*SPX_N`-byte seeds + all-`0x00` + all-`0xFF`; compares `pk[2N]` **and** `sk[4N]` | `b42_seed_keypair` | [x] |\n| **B43** | `crypto_sign_signature` + `crypto_sign_verify` | `mlen ∈ {0,1,2,15,16,17,31,32,33,47,48,49,55,56,57,63,64,65,71,72,73,103,104,105,127,128,129,135,136,137,167,168,169,255,256,257,1000}` (spans every backend's block/rate boundary) × keys from random seeds; the DRBG is re-seeded identically for C and Rust before **each** call, so the non-deterministic `optrand` is made deterministic and the signatures must be byte-identical; then both `.so`s must accept both signatures | `b43_signature_verify` | [x] |\n| **B44** | `crypto_sign` + `crypto_sign_open` | same message lengths; compares `sm[SPX_BYTES+mlen]`, `*smlen`, and the recovered `m`/`*mlen` | `b44_sign_open` | [x] |\n| **B45** | `crypto_sign_keypair` | `randombytes_init` with the same entropy for both `.so`s ⇒ the \"random\" key pair must be byte-identical; 32 different entropy inputs | `b45_keypair` | [x] |\n| **B46** | `randombytes_init` + `randombytes` + `DRBG_ctx` | 32 random `(entropy[48], personalization[48] or NULL)` × `xlen ∈ {0,1,15,16,17,31,32,33,48,49,64,100}`, called repeatedly so the DRBG advances; compares the output **and** the exported `DRBG_ctx` global (`Key[32] ‖ V[16] ‖ reseed_counter`) | `b46_drbg` | [x] |\n| **B47** | `AES256_ECB` | 512 random `(key[32], ctr[16])` — the raw AES-256-ECB block that the Rust reimplements without OpenSSL | `b47_aes256_ecb` | [x] |\n| **B48** | `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update` | 512 random `(Key[32], V[16])` × `provided_data ∈ {NULL, random[48]}`; compares the updated `Key` and `V` | `b48_drbg_update` | [x] |\n| **B49** | `seedexpander_init` + `seedexpander` | 64 random `(seed[32], diversifier[8])` × `maxlen ∈ {1,16,17,48,1000,0x7FFFFFFF,0xFFFFFFFF}` × a sequence of `xlen ∈ {1,5,15,16,17,31,32,33}` requests that drives `buffer_pos` through every value; compares the output bytes **and** the whole `AES_XOF_struct` after each call | `b49_seedexpander` | [x] |\n| **B31b** | `SPX_wots_pk_from_sig` at `gen_chain`'s extremes | all-`0x00` message (every base-w digit `0` ⇒ `steps = SPX_WOTS_W-1`, maximum chain work) and all-`0xFF` (every digit `W-1` ⇒ `steps = 0`, no chain work), plus `0x0F`/`0xF0` patterns; asserts the extremes really are extreme via the C's own `chain_lengths` | `b31b_wots_pk_from_sig_chain_extremes` | [x] |\n| **B46b** | `randombytes` + `DRBG_ctx` with **crafted** state | all 17 \"k trailing `0xff` bytes\" patterns of `DRBG_ctx.V` (every depth of the byte-15→0 carry loop of `rng.c:160-167`, including the full 128-bit wrap), each with a `0xfe` variant and 32 randomized near-carry states, × `xlen ∈ {0,1,15,16,17,32,48}`; plus `reseed_counter ∈ {0, 1, INT_MAX-1, INT_MAX, -1, INT_MIN}` (signed `++` overflow). Reachable only by writing the exported `DRBG_ctx` symbol directly — 2^8…2^128 API calls otherwise | `b46b_randombytes_v_carry_chain` | [x] |\n| **B49b** | `seedexpander` with **crafted** `AES_XOF_struct` | 26 `ctr[12..16]` patterns covering every depth of the byte-15→**12** carry loop of `rng.c:91-98` (including `ff ff ff ff`, where the carry falls off the end of the loop and is dropped) × `buffer_pos ∈ {0,1,5,8,15,16}` × `xlen ∈ {1,16,40,100}`, plus an 8-request sequence from each state so many carries happen in a row | `b49b_seedexpander_ctr_carry_chain` | [x] |\n| **B50** | full KAT transcript (`crypto_sign_keypair` + `crypto_sign` + `crypto_sign_open` over the NIST KAT loop) | the exact `PQCgenKAT_sign.c` schedule: `randombytes_init(seed_i)` for 100 iterations, `mlen = 33*(i+1)`; compares every intermediate `pk`, `sk`, `sm`, `smlen`, `m1`, `mlen1` between C and Rust | `b50_kat_transcript` | [x] |\n\n## How the rows are executed\n\n```sh\n./scripts/build_c.sh    <backend> <thash> <secpar>   # cmake -> c_builds/<cfg>/\nCARGO_TARGET_DIR=target/features/<cfg> \\\n  cargo test --release --no-default-features --features \"<backend>,<thash>,<secpar>\"\n./scripts/sweep_test.sh                              # all 48 combinations\n./scripts/sweep_test.sh blake simple                 # a subset\nSPX_TEST_LEVEL=2 cargo test --release ...            # 8x more iterations\n```\n\nTest files:\n\n| file | rows |\n|---|---|\n| `tests/isolation.rs`      | the symbol-interposition proof (see below) |\n| `tests/phase_b_core.rs`   | B01–B05, B27, B32–B34, B41 |\n| `tests/phase_b_hash.rs`   | B06–B26 |\n| `tests/phase_b_high.rs`   | B28–B31, B35–B40, B42–B50 |\n| `tests/phase_c_errors.rs` | every `ERRORS.md` row |\n\n**⚠ `--no-default-features` is mandatory.**  `src/params.rs` (and\n`tests/common/cfg.rs`, which mirrors it) resolves the security parameter by a\nfixed priority `128s > 128f > 192s > 192f > 256s > 256f`, and `Cargo.toml`'s\n`default = [\"blake\", \"simple\", \"128f\"]` would otherwise out-rank e.g. `192s`.\nAll scripts in `scripts/` pass `--no-default-features`.\n\n## Why the harness needs `RTLD_DEEPBIND`\n\nThe C `.so`s and the Rust `.so` export the *same* symbol names.  `readelf -r`\nshows the Rust cdylib carries `R_X86_64_GLOB_DAT` relocations against its **own**\nexported symbols (`SPX_thash`, `SPX_wots_treehashx1`, `SPX_fors_sign`,\n`crypto_sign_verify`, `AES256_ECB`, `DRBG_ctx`, …), so its internal calls go\nthrough the GOT and would be **interposed** by a C library earlier in the\nloader's global scope — silently making every \"Rust\" result come from the C code.\n\n`tests/isolation.rs` proves this: it builds a poison `.so` with a deliberately\nwrong `SPX_thash`/`SPX_wots_treehashx1`, and shows\n\n* poison + no `RTLD_DEEPBIND` ⇒ the Rust result **changes** (the hazard is real),\n* poison + `RTLD_DEEPBIND`    ⇒ the Rust result is **unchanged**.\n\n`tests/common/mod.rs` therefore opens the Rust cdylib **first** with\n`RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL | RTLD_DEEPBIND`, and only then brings the C objects into\nthe global scope (`libcrypto` → `libsphincs_core_det.so` `RTLD_LAZY|RTLD_GLOBAL`\n→ `lib<backend>.so` `RTLD_NOW|RTLD_GLOBAL`, which is exactly the order the C\n`driver` binary binds them; the two C objects have *mutually* undefined symbols\nand neither has a `DT_NEEDED` for the other).\n\n## Independent end-to-end cross-check\n\nBesides the `.so`-level rows above, `scripts/driver_digests.sh <cfg>` runs the C\n`driver` executable (`app/src/PQCgenKAT_sign.c`, 7 KAT iterations,\n`BASE_MLEN=33`) and the Rust `driver` binary and compares the printed\n`KAT transcript digest`.  This exercises the whole\n`randombytes_init → crypto_sign_keypair → crypto_sign → crypto_sign_open`\npipeline plus the backend-specific transcript hash, through a completely\ndifferent code path from the tests.\n\n## Results\n\n`target/sweep_test.txt` — `PASS` for all 48 combinations (76 tests each).\n`target/driver_digests.txt` — identical KAT digests for all 48 combinations.\n\n--- symbols summary ---\n# SYMBOLS.md — dynamic-symbol parity between the C `.so`s and the Rust `.so`\n\nDerived mechanically from `nm -D --defined-only` on the C shared libraries and\non `libsphincs_plus.so`.\n\n## How the C build partitions the symbols\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` + `c_src/app/CMakeLists.txt` + `c_src/lib/<HB>/CMakeLists.txt`\nproduce **three** shared objects per configuration:\n\n| C shared object | sources | notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `app/libsphincs_core.so`     | `address.c fors.c merkle.c sign.c utils.c utilsx1.c wots.c wotsx1.c` + `randombytes.c` | non-deterministic `randombytes` (`/dev/urandom`), returns `void` |\n| `app/libsphincs_core_det.so` | same core + `rng.c`                                                                    | NIST AES-256-CTR-DRBG `randombytes`, returns `int`; this is what `driver` links |\n| `lib/<HB>/lib<HB>.so`        | the hash backend + (`blake`/`sha2` only) a second copy of `app/src/utils.c`            | `SPX_thash`, `SPX_prf_addr`, … |\n\nThe Rust crate is a **single** `cdylib`, so it must export the *union* of the\nthree C symbol sets.  Because C cannot have two `randombytes` in one object, the\nunion keeps the *deterministic* `rng.c` version (that is the one the KAT driver\nlinks and the one `sign.c` calls); the `randombytes.c` translation lives in\n`src/randombytes.rs` under the non-exported name `randombytes_urandom`\n(documented in that file).\n\n## Reproducing the check\n\n```sh\n./scripts/build_c.sh    <backend> <thash> <secpar>   # -> c_builds/<cfg>/\n./scripts/build_rust.sh <backend> <thash> <secpar>   # -> target/features/<cfg>/\n./scripts/symdiff.sh    <backend> <thash> <secpar>   # prints MISSING[...] or OK[...]\n./scripts/sweep_build.sh                             # all 48 combinations\n```\n\n## Result\n\n`target/sweep_build.txt` shows `OK[<cfg>] N C symbols all present` for **all 48**\nfeature combinations — i.e. **0 missing symbols**, and the Rust `.so` has no\nundefined non-libc symbols (`nm -D --undefined-only` lists only glibc/`ld.so`\nentries; see `scripts/undef_check.sh`).\n\n## Fixes applied during this verification\n\n| symbol | C definition | why it was missing | fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `cst` | `lib/blake/src/blake512.c:45` — `const u64 cst[16]` (**no** `static`, unlike `blake256.c:41` which *is* `static`) → external linkage, `R` | Rust had `static cst: [u64;16]` without `#[no_mangle]` | added `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub static cst` in `src/blake/blake512.rs` |\n| `DRBG_ctx` | `app/src/rng.c:15` — `AES256_CTR_DRBG_struct DRBG_ctx;` → external linkage, `B` | Rust had `pub static mut DRBG_ctx` without `#[no_mangle]` | added `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` in `src/rng.rs` |\n\nNo symbol needed a *new* implementation: every C translation unit\n(`address.c fors.c merkle.c sign.c utils.c utilsx1.c wots.c wotsx1.c\nrandombytes.c rng.c`, plus all four backends' `hash_*.c`, `thash_*_robust.c`,\n`thash_*_simple.c`, `blake256.c blake512.c sha2.c fips202.c haraka.c`) already\nhad a corresponding Rust module.  Nothing is stubbed.\n\n## Symbol inventory\n\n### A. Core, present in **every** configuration\n\nFrom `app/src/{address,fors,merkle,sign,utils,utilsx1,wots,wotsx1}.c`.\n`app/include/*.h` wrap most names in `#define x SPX_NAMESPACE(x)` and\n`params-*.h` defines `SPX_NAMESPACE(s) => SPX_##s`, hence the `SPX_` prefix.\nThe `api.h` entry points are **not** namespaced.\n\n| symbol | type | C source | Rust source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `SPX_set_layer_addr`    | T | `address.c:11`  | `src/address.rs` |\n| `SPX_set_tree_addr`     | T | `address.c:19`  | `src/address.rs` |\n| `SPX_set_type`          | T | `address.c:33`  | `src/address.rs` |\n| `SPX_copy_subtree_addr` | T | `address.c:42`  | `src/address.rs` |\n| `SPX_set_keypair_addr`  | T | `address.c:53`  | `src/address.rs` |\n| `SPX_copy_keypair_addr` | T | `address.c:62`  | `src/address.rs` |\n| `SPX_set_chain_addr`    | T | `address.c:72`  | `src/address.rs` |\n| `SPX_set_hash_addr`     | T | `address.c:81`  | `src/address.rs` |\n| `SPX_set_tree_height`   | T | `address.c:92`  | `src/address.rs` |\n| `SPX_set_tree_index`    | T | `address.c:101` | `src/address.rs` |\n| `SPX_ull_to_bytes`      | T | `utils.c:12`    | `src/utils.rs` |\n| `SPX_u32_to_bytes`      | T | `utils.c:24`    | `src/utils.rs` |\n| `SPX_bytes_to_ull`      | T | `utils.c:35`    | `src/utils.rs` |\n| `SPX_compute_root`      | T | `utils.c:50`    | `src/utils.rs` |\n| `SPX_treehash`          | T | `utils.c:105`   | `src/utils.rs` |\n| `SPX_wots_treehashx1`   | T | `utilsx1.c:24`  | `src/utilsx1.rs` |\n| `SPX_fors_treehashx1`   | T | `utilsx1.c:99`  | `src/utilsx1.rs` |\n| `SPX_chain_lengths`     | T | `wots.c:87`     | `src/wots.rs` |\n| `SPX_wots_pk_from_sig`  | T | `wots.c:98`     | `src/wots.rs` |\n| `SPX_wots_gen_leafx1`   | T | `wotsx1.c:17`   | `src/wotsx1.rs` |\n| `SPX_fors_gen_leafx1`   | T | `fors.c:26`     | `src/fors.rs` |\n| `SPX_fors_sign`         | T | `fors.c:66`     | `src/fors.rs` |\n| `SPX_fors_pk_from_sig`  | T | `fors.c:119`    | `src/fors.rs` |\n| `SPX_merkle_sign`       | T | `merkle.c:18`   | `src/merkle.rs` |\n| `SPX_merkle_gen_root`   | T | `merkle.c:45`   | `src/merkle.rs` |\n| `crypto_sign_secretkeybytes` | T | `sign.c:19`  | `src/sign.rs` |\n| `crypto_sign_publickeybytes` | T | `sign.c:27`  | `src/sign.rs` |\n| `crypto_sign_bytes`          | T | `sign.c:35`  | `src/sign.rs` |\n| `crypto_sign_seedbytes`      | T | `sign.c:43`  | `src/sign.rs` |\n| `crypto_sign_seed_keypair`   | T | `sign.c:53`  | `src/sign.rs` |\n| `crypto_sign_keypair`        | T | `sign.c:83`  | `src/sign.rs` |\n| `crypto_sign_signature`      | T | `sign.c:95`  | `src/sign.rs` |\n| `crypto_sign_verify`         | T | `sign.c:163` | `src/sign.rs` |\n| `crypto_sign`                | T | `sign.c:246` | `src/sign.rs` |\n| `crypto_sign_open`           | T | `sign.c:263` | `src/sign.rs` |\n| `randombytes`           | T | `rng.c:153` (det.) / `randombytes.c:12` | `src/rng.rs` (det.); `src/randombytes.rs` holds the urandom variant |\n| `randombytes_init`      | T | `rng.c:137`     | `src/rng.rs` |\n| `seedexpander_init`     | T | `rng.c:27`      | `src/rng.rs` |\n| `seedexpander`          | T | `rng.c:62`      | `src/rng.rs` |\n| `AES256_ECB`            | T | `rng.c:117`     | `src/rng.rs` |\n| `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update`| T | `rng.c:186`     | `src/rng.rs` |\n| `DRBG_ctx`              | **B** | `rng.c:15`  | `src/rng.rs` |\n\n### B. `HASH_BACKEND=blake` — `lib/blake/libblake.so`\n\n| symbol | type | C source | Rust source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `SPX_initialize_hash_function` | T | `hash_blake.c:29` | `src/blake/hash_blake.rs` |\n| `SPX_prf_addr`                 | T | `hash_blake.c:37` | `src/blake/hash_blake.rs` |\n| `SPX_gen_message_random`       | T | `hash_blake.c:56` | `src/blake/hash_blake.rs` |\n| `SPX_hash_message`             | T | `hash_blake.c:76` | `src/blake/hash_blake.rs` |\n| `SPX_thash`                    | T | `thash_blake_{robust,simple}.c:19` | `src/blake/thash_blake_{robust,simple}.rs` |\n| `blake256_compress`            | T | `blake256.c:53`   | `src/blake/blake256.rs` |\n| `blake256_init`                | T | `blake256.c:285`  | `src/blake/blake256.rs` |\n| `blake256_update`              | T | `blake256.c:300`  | `src/blake/blake256.rs` |\n| `blake256_final`               | T | `blake256.c:331`  | `src/blake/blake256.rs` |\n| `SPX_blake256_mgf1`            | T | `blake256.c:372`  | `src/blake/blake256.rs` |\n| `blake256`                     | T | `blake256.c:395`  | `src/blake/blake256.rs` |\n| `blake512_compress`            | T | `blake512.c:60`   | `src/blake/blake512.rs` |\n| `blake512_init`                | T | `blake512.c:295`  | `src/blake/blake512.rs` |\n| `blake512_update`              | T | `blake512.c:309`  | `src/blake/blake512.rs` |\n| `blake512_final`               | T | `blake512.c:338`  | `src/blake/blake512.rs` |\n| `SPX_blake512_mgf1`            | T | `blake512.c:379`  | `src/blake/blake512.rs` |\n| `blake512`                     | T | `blake512.c:402`  | `src/blake/blake512.rs` |\n| `cst`                          | **R** | `blake512.c:45` | `src/blake/blake512.rs` |\n| `SPX_ull_to_bytes` `SPX_u32_to_bytes` `SPX_bytes_to_ull` `SPX_compute_root` `SPX_treehash` | T | second copy of `app/src/utils.c` pulled into `libblake.so` by `lib/blake/CMakeLists.txt` | same Rust `src/utils.rs` (one copy suffices) |\n\n### C. `HASH_BACKEND=sha2` — `lib/sha2/libsha2.so`\n\n| symbol | type | C source | Rust source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `SPX_initialize_hash_function` `SPX_prf_addr` `SPX_gen_message_random` `SPX_hash_message` | T | `hash_sha2.c` | `src/sha2/hash_sha2.rs` |\n| `SPX_thash` | T | `thash_sha2_{robust,simple}.c` | `src/sha2/thash_sha2_{robust,simple}.rs` |\n| `sha256` `sha256_inc_init` `sha256_inc_blocks` `sha256_inc_finalize` | T | `sha2.c` | `src/sha2/sha2.rs` |\n| `sha512` `sha512_inc_init` `sha512_inc_blocks` `sha512_inc_finalize` | T | `sha2.c` | `src/sha2/sha2.rs` |\n| `SPX_mgf1_256` `SPX_mgf1_512` `SPX_seed_state` | T | `sha2.c` | `src/sha2/sha2.rs` |\n| `SPX_ull_to_bytes` `SPX_u32_to_bytes` `SPX_bytes_to_ull` `SPX_compute_root` `SPX_treehash` | T | second copy of `app/src/utils.c` | `src/utils.rs` |\n\n### D. `HASH_BACKEND=shake` — `lib/shake/libshake.so`\n\n| symbol | type | C source | Rust source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `SPX_initialize_hash_function` `SPX_prf_addr` `SPX_gen_message_random` `SPX_hash_message` | T | `hash_shake.c` | `src/shake/hash_shake.rs` |\n| `SPX_thash` | T | `thash_shake_{robust,simple}.c` | `src/shake/thash_shake_{robust,simple}.rs` |\n| `shake256` `shake256_absorb` `shake256_squeezeblocks` | T | `fips202.c` | `src/shake/fips202.rs` |\n| `shake256_inc_init` `shake256_inc_absorb` `shake256_inc_finalize` `shake256_inc_squeeze` | T | `fips202.c` | `src/shake/fips202.rs` |\n\n(`lib/shake/CMakeLists.txt` does **not** pull in `app/src/utils.c`, so\n`libshake.so` has no `SPX_*_to_bytes` / `SPX_treehash`; those come from\n`libsphincs_core*.so` only.)\n\n### E. `HASH_BACKEND=haraka` — `lib/haraka/libharaka.so`\n\n| symbol | type | C source | Rust source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `SPX_initialize_hash_function` `SPX_prf_addr` `SPX_gen_message_random` `SPX_hash_message` | T | `hash_haraka.c` | `src/haraka/hash_haraka.rs` |\n| `SPX_thash` | T | `thash_haraka_{robust,simple}.c` | `src/haraka/thash_haraka_{robust,simple}.rs` |\n| `SPX_tweak_constants` `SPX_haraka512_perm` `SPX_haraka512` `SPX_haraka256` `SPX_haraka_S` | T | `haraka.c` | `src/haraka/haraka.rs` |\n| `SPX_haraka_S_inc_init` `SPX_haraka_S_inc_absorb` `SPX_haraka_S_inc_finalize` `SPX_haraka_S_inc_squeeze` | T | `haraka.c` | `src/haraka/haraka.rs` |\n\n(`libharaka.so` also does not include `app/src/utils.c`